; NCX example: mill-turn with main spindle, sub spindle and milling spindle in one channel. Turning, transfer to the sub spindle, milling.
; Machine words (roles MAIN, SUB, TOOL, TURRET1; axis Z2; functions SUB_CHUCK, MAIN_CHUCK) come from millturn1.toml (machine-config.md).
; No source program: this example is written by hand to show the words; the Siemens equivalents are given as comments.
FILE=BEGIN NCX=1
PROGRAM=BEGIN NAME="SHAFT_TRANSFER" CHANNEL=1
FEED_MODE=PER_REV COMP=OFF UNITS=MM WORKPLANE=ZX DIAMETER=ON CYCLE=OFF
ORIGIN=1                                                ; G54

SECTION="TURN OD"
TOOL:TURRET1=3 OFFSET:LEN=3 OFFSET:RAD=3                ; T3 D3
SPINDLE:MAIN=CW RPM:MAIN=1500                           ; S1500 M3   (S1 is the master spindle of millturn1.toml; S1=1500 M1=3 on a machine with another master)
RAPID X=42 Z=2                                          ; G0 X42 Z2
LINE X=40 F=0.2                                         ; G1 X40 F0.2
LINE Z=-60                                              ; G1 Z-60
RAPID X=45                                              ; G0 X45

SECTION="TRANSFER"
SPINDLE_SYNC=MAIN,SUB                                   ; COUPON(S2,S1)
FUNC:SUB_CHUCK=OPEN                                     ; M68 (from the machine configuration)
RAPID Z2=-58                                            ; G0 Z2=-58   (sub spindle axis)
FUNC:SUB_CHUCK=CLOSE                                    ; M69, marks the handover for the reader rule (D40)
FUNC:MAIN_CHUCK=OPEN                                    ; M66
SPINDLE_SYNC=OFF                                        ; COUPOF(S2,S1)
SPINDLE:MAIN=OFF                                        ; M5
WORKPIECE=SUB                                           ; from here the part is in the sub spindle
ORIGIN=2                                                ; G55

SECTION="MILL FLAT"
SPINDLE_MODE:SUB=AXIS                                   ; M2=70 / SPOS
TOOL:TURRET1=12 OFFSET:LEN=12 OFFSET:RAD=12 SPINDLE:TOOL=CW RPM:TOOL=6000   ; T12 D12, S3=6000 M3=3
FEED_MODE=PER_MIN                                       ; G94
RAPID X=20 C=0                                          ; C is the axis of the current workpiece holder, here C2
RAPID Z2=-5
LINE C=90 F=300                                         ; G1 C2=90 F300
RAPID Z2=10
SPINDLE:TOOL=OFF                                        ; M3=5
PROGRAM=END                                             ; M30
FILE=END                                                ; end of file

; Notes
; 1. DIAMETER=ON: X=40 is a diameter; the VM stores the radius 20.
; 2. The transfer is machine functions and motions around SPINDLE_SYNC and WORKPIECE; NCX does not model it as one command.
; 3. Z2 is a machine axis named in the program on purpose; a program that addresses the sub spindle axis is machine specific by intent (D30).
; 4. After WORKPIECE=SUB the coordinates are in the sub spindle's own frame, +Z out of its chuck toward the tool (D57); whether the machine mirrors Z or uses a datum with the opposite Z is a configuration setting.
